# NYXUS · Calamares branding descriptor · Suxyn edition
---
componentName: nyxus

welcomeStyleCalamares: true
welcomeExpandingLogo:  false
windowExpanding:       normal
windowSize:            900px,560px
windowPlacement:       center

# ── strings · VOICE_AND_COPY §1, the naming law ─────────────────────────────
# "Casing is fixed and never varies. Write these exactly: NYXUS · Nyxus Suxyn ·
# jeTT · Bifrost · Meli · Arsenal · PRISM · Kage Ryu … One canonical spelling in
# a lookup table, referenced by every surface — including the About screen, THE
# INSTALLER, GRUB, and every log line."
# `Suxyn` alone and `NYXUS Suxyn` are neither of the two canonical forms. The
# product is `NYXUS`; the edition is `Nyxus Suxyn`. Fixed here (2026-08-17).
#
# NO KERNEL NAME IN THESE STRINGS. VOICE_AND_COPY §5's installer deck shows
# "NYXUS 2026.08 · Kage Ryu 6.14.2", but the ISO does NOT ship that kernel by
# default: WIP-80 closed with build-iso.sh defaulting NYX_WITH_KAGE_RYU to 0, and
# HANDOFF's settled decision is stock Arch for v1. Printing a kernel the default
# bake does not install would put a fabricated fact on the first screen a new
# user reads, so the version line stays edition-only. If the kernel default ever
# flips, this is the line that follows it.
#
# ⚠ THE VERSION IS NOT WRITTEN HERE. IT IS STAMPED AT BAKE. (TRK-3687)
# Observed on real hardware 2026-09-01: the welcome page read "Welcome to the
# Calamares installer for Nyxus Suxyn · 2026.08" while the stick it was running
# from was `nyxus-suxyn-2026.09.01`. The string had been correct when it was
# typed and had been a lie on every bake since — which is what a hand-pinned
# version always becomes, because nothing recomputes it and no gate could tell
# a stale month from a current one.
# The three version strings carry the token `__ISO_DATE__`. `build-iso.sh`
# substitutes the SAME date that names the ISO file and stamps profiledef.sh
# iso_version and os-release IMAGE_VERSION. The bake ABORTS if any token
# survives, so a broken stamp is loud on the build box instead of quiet on
# a user's screen. `productName`/`shortProductName` stay literal.
strings:
    productName:         "Nyxus Suxyn"
    shortProductName:    "Nyxus Suxyn"
    version:             "Nyxus Suxyn · __ISO_DATE__"
    shortVersion:        "__ISO_DATE__"
    versionedName:       "Nyxus Suxyn · __ISO_DATE__"
    shortVersionedName:  "Nyxus Suxyn"
    bootloaderEntryName: "Nyxus Suxyn"
    productUrl:          "https://ikswognereisj-ctrl.github.io/Nyxus-Suxyn/"
    supportUrl:          "https://github.com/ikswognereisj-ctrl/Nyxus-Suxyn"
    knownIssuesUrl:      "https://github.com/ikswognereisj-ctrl/Nyxus-Suxyn/issues"
    releaseNotesUrl:     "https://ikswognereisj-ctrl.github.io/Nyxus-Suxyn/"
    donateUrl:           ""

images:
    productLogo:    "logo.png"
    productIcon:    "logo.png"
    productWelcome: "welcome.png"

slideshow:           "show.qml"
slideshowAPI:        2

# ── the style keys this Calamares actually reads (2026-08-13) ───────────────
# The old lowercase names (sidebarBackground, sidebarTextSelect,
# sidebarTextHighlight, sidebarBackgroundSelected) are a pre-3.3 schema. The
# shipped 3.3.15 logs "Unknown branding *style* entry" for every one of them
# and falls back to unset colors — which painted the non-current step names
# near-black on the near-black sidebar. That is why the installer appeared to
# show only the current step: Welcome, Location, Partitions, Users, Summary,
# Install were all there, invisible. Verified against the binary itself:
# `strings /usr/lib/libcalamares*` lists exactly these four Sidebar keys.
#
# ── THE STEP LIST · rev 3 §A3, and the four keys are the whole vocabulary ────
# THIS IS THE PROGRESS LIST. Calamares gives branding exactly four sidebar
# colours — no alpha, no left bar, no per-state hooks — so §A3's selected nav
# item ("glass-control-active fill (cyan at 0.13) + 2px left bar in cyan +
# glow-sm … NOT a solid magenta pill") cannot be built as specified. What IS
# available is the hue and the inversion, so the chip takes §A3's cyan.
#
# WHAT CHANGED AND WHY, measured:
#   SidebarBackground        #03040c → #020506  `_swirl._emission.base.void`
#     was a MIRROR of void, not `_palette_fixed.void`. #020506 is the value
#     `_tokens.edges.ground.token` names as THE GROUND, which is the bed every
#     contrast figure in accent.json is measured against — so the sidebar now
#     sits on the bed the authority assumes. Luminance moves 0.00133 → 0.00135:
#     visually identical, and now on-token.
#   SidebarBackgroundCurrent #edf1ff → #0aa2d6  A NEAR-WHITE SLAB was the
#     loudest break on the first screen a new user sees: `_palette_fixed.text`
#     used as a large filled area, luminance 0.881 against
#     `_tokens.ambient.peak_luminance_max` 0.45 — 96% over the clamp, and
#     _findings.peak_luminance_breach rules anything over it "UNSAFE AS ANY
#     FILLED AREA". Teal is `_palette_fixed.teal` = `accent-interactive`, which
#     is §A3's cyan, and it is a SELECTED state, i.e. ladder B, so it is subject
#     to the 3:1 component floor and clears it at 6.96:1 on the ground.
#   SidebarTextCurrent       #03040c → #020506  the ground, on the teal chip:
#     6.96:1, over the 4.5:1 text floor.
#   SidebarText              unchanged. #edf1ff on the ground is 18.14:1.
#
# NOT A TINT, AND SAID OUT LOUD: §1.1 wants control-active to be "a tint, never
# an opaque fill". These keys take a bare colour and the sidebar is an opaque
# widget with nothing behind it, so a tint would have to be pre-composited into
# a new hex — which is exactly the invention this palette forbids. A solid stop
# at the right hue is the honest option the schema leaves.
#
# UNSEEN: no photograph of this sidebar with a teal current-step chip exists.
# The 08-13 evidence is of the near-white chip.
#
# 2026-08-21 (PF) took SidebarBackgroundCurrent to the periwinkle mix of
# that morning's PERIWINKLE + GLACIER ruling. WITHDRAWN 2026-08-22 (TRK-1460):
# the owner rejected that colour on tty1 and ordered the build to ship the
# palette of the last baked ISO, 87da09fe, and nothing else. The current step
# is back to teal `_palette_fixed.teal` = accent-interactive, the value the
# bake carries and the reasoning above already measures: ladder B, 6.96:1 on
# the ground, and SidebarTextCurrent #020506 on it at the same 6.96:1.
# The four periwinkle hexes are forbidden tree-wide by gate 13t80.
style:
    SidebarBackground:        "#020506"
    SidebarText:              "#b7e6f2"
    SidebarBackgroundCurrent: "#ff7847"
    SidebarTextCurrent:       "#020506"
